{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795375216,"nonce":"a685qm2husFW8kqU7JDdHMKZy00=","title":"Desktop AOT builds ignore --native-lib and load HDLLs at run time","message":"On macOS, Linux and Windows, `ash --build X --native-lib libgreeter.a main.hl` ignores the archive. The program names an HDLL, so aot_build.rs takes the SHARED runtime, stages libhl beside the binary, and resolves natives with dlopen at run time. The executable is the same size with or without the archive, and with greeter.hdll moved away it fails with \"Native library 'greeter' not loaded\".\n\nAndroid and iOS link the same archives into one image: TargetAbi.static_natives is set for phone triples, the build resolves each primitive through a weak hlp_\u003cprim\u003e reference (aot_data.rs, hlp_aot_native_linked), and the static runtime is used whatever the program names.\n\nWanted (from the hxn session, which makes AOT the desktop default for hxn run hl): when every HDLL the program names is given as a --native-lib archive, link the static runtime and resolve those natives from the archives, giving one executable with no .hdll or libhl beside it. An HDLL named but not given as an archive keeps the run-time path, and the build keeps the shared runtime in that case.\n\nWhy the HDLL path exists on desktop: a prebuilt .hdll brings its own copy of the runtime, so the binary must share one runtime or two collectors meet. An archive built against ash's runtime has no second copy, so that reason does not apply to it.\n\nThe decision is per target today (target_abi.rs sets static_natives only for android and ios, and module.rs computes aot_shared_runtime from the natives alone). It has to become per build: static_natives and the shared-runtime choice depend on whether the archives cover every non-runtime native. ash_cli main.rs already filters the natives with archive::defined_symbols for phone builds; the same filter would run on desktop when coverage is complete.\n\nReproducer: ~/Vibranium/hxn/examples/greeter, run hxn run hl --ash \u003cash\u003e. Check: nm on the executable shows hlp_greeter_* after the change, and the build runs with greeter.hdll and libhl.dylib removed.","files":null}]}